What ships
----------

The engine (engine/src), the root module (module/) and the app (app/) are original ResonanceFX
work, GPL-3.0-or-later. The DSP core in engine/src/core comes from Basilar, also by Xeloria and
also GPL-3.0-or-later. See docs/LICENSING.md for how the engine was written and what it does
and doesn't contain.

Third-party data
----------------

Head-related impulse responses in engine/src/core/src/data/KemarHrir.cpp are derived from the
MIT KEMAR measurements: W. G. Gardner and K. D. Martin, "HRTF Measurements of a KEMAR Dummy-Head
Microphone", MIT Media Lab Perceptual Computing Technical Report #280, 1994. Free to use with
this citation.

Headphone profiles in app/app/src/main/assets/autoeq/profiles.json are generated from the
AutoEq project (https://github.com/jaakkopasanen/AutoEq), Copyright (c) 2018-2022 Jaakko
Pasanen, MIT License (reproduced in app/app/src/main/assets/autoeq/LICENSE and shown in the
app under Settings > Open-source licenses). Measurements by their respective sources
(oratory1990, crinacle, Rtings and others) as credited in AutoEq.

The root module's installer conventions follow the Magisk module template (Zackptg5 and
contributors); module/META-INF/com/google/android/update-binary is an original minimal stub.
